@startuml
!theme plain
title Data Ingestion — Validation, Classification, Versioning and Indexing
actor User
participant "Unified Work Area" as UI
participant "API Gateway" as API
participant "Identity & Scope" as IAM
participant "Bulk Ingestion" as ING
participant "Malware Scanner" as AV
participant "Metadata & Rights Validator" as VAL
participant "Version & Provenance" as VER
database PostgreSQL as PG
collections "Object Storage" as OBJ
participant "Text/Media Extractor" as EXT
participant "Vector Index" as VEC
participant "Search Index" as SEARCH
participant "Audit Service" as AUDIT

User -> UI: Select files/folder/ZIP and target scope
UI -> API: Create upload batch + manifest
API -> IAM: Authorise upload action and scope
IAM --> API: Permit with effective role/scope
API -> ING: Create quarantined batch
ING -> AUDIT: Record batch creation
loop Each item
  ING -> AV: Scan bytes
  AV --> ING: clean / blocked
  alt blocked or unsupported
    ING -> PG: Save rejected item and reason
    ING -> AUDIT: Record rejection
  else clean
    ING -> VAL: Validate metadata, classification and rights
    alt metadata incomplete or rights unclear
      VAL --> ING: quarantine + required remediation
      ING -> PG: Save quarantined item
    else admissible
      VAL --> ING: validated
      ING -> VER: Resolve duplicate/version relationship
      VER -> PG: Create content item or append version
      VER -> OBJ: Store immutable object version
      VER --> ING: version_id + provenance
      ING -> EXT: Extract text/transcript/structure
      EXT --> ING: extracted content + quality signals
      ING -> VEC: Upsert tenant- and scope-filtered embeddings
      ING -> SEARCH: Upsert exact/faceted index
      ING -> PG: Mark item ready or review_required
      ING -> AUDIT: Record provenance and state change
    end
  end
end
ING --> API: Batch summary, errors and decisions
API --> UI: Show per-item outcomes and remediation actions
@enduml
